==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Brainwashed Dragon Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Brainwashed King Dragon Cat''' after obtaining from [[Spitting Death (Merciless)]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
With the exception of health and damage, which are level dependent, this unit is the exact same as [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]], with literally no differences in any aspect. Brainwashed Dragon Cat is thus best used in place of King Dragon as a relatively spammable long range attacker for tough foes with also some range, like [[The Face]]. Note that this variant needs level 46 to surpass its base form's level 20+90 stats, and level 43 to surpass Manic King Dragon's level 50 stats. This allows for it to be incredibly useful in [[Empire of Cats]], where it can deal much more damage due to having higher stats then a level 10 Dragon Cat.

Of course, this unit's real selling point, as a copy of another, is the ability to combine it with King Dragon Cat, [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon Cat]] and/or [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon]] to effectively cut on the recharge time a lot more than how much combos would allow, resulting in massive DPS; this is a good strategy for stages like [[Revenge of Red Sky (Merciless)|Revenge of Red Sky]].

As you reach the later parts of the game, specifically [[Uncanny Legends]], however, this unit becomes much less useful. As with most other of his equivalents, Brainwashed Lizard's single target and high cost means it can be infeasible to accumulate them on many stages when specialist units already offer much more for the same price or less. And unlike [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon]], whose [[Talents]] provide it with several additional attributes that distinguish it from stackable attackers, Brainwashed Lizard has no niche or specialization to begin with nor outstanding stats to compensate.

=== '''True Form''' ===
Brainwashed King Dragon Cat becomes a surprisingly powerful backliner with his new immunities. He is now similar to talented [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Dancer Cat]]/[[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]], those three are immune to Waves and Freeze and inflict high ranged DPS. However, Brainwashed King Dragon Cat has higher range than the rest of the three, allow him to be more sufficient in some situations. If you stack two Brainwashed King Dragon Cats, they surpass [[Miyamoku Musashi (Special Cat)|Awakened Musashi]]'s DPS, surprisingly. Considering that, Brainwashed King Dragon Cat is a rather competent backliner.

There are a lot of pros for Brainwashed King Dragon Cat as a spammable anti-Wave attacker: he has decent survivability and good range, basically a weak version of Awakened Musashi for being pretty disposable. Although Dancer Cat and Hitman Cat outclass them in most situations, those three can be used to annihilate any Wave enemies by being spammed, thus Brainwashed King Dragon Cat is very accessible, as he doesn't need any NP or Behemoth Stones to carry immunities to Waves and Freeze, just beating his overall easy awakening stage if you have some nice anti-Aku like [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]], [[Rugby Cat (Rare Cat)|Gridiron Cat]] or [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]]. Overall this True Form is a satisfactory, providing you another stackable Wave-immune damage dealer.

